{"question_id": "caf03d32", "hypothesis": "A few things that make the biggest difference in slow cooker results, tailored to what you've been working with:\n\n**Liquid is the #1 issue.** Slow cookers barely evaporate. If you're adapting a stovetop recipe, cut the liquid by about a third. A stew that's soupy at the end almost always started with too much broth. You can always thin it out, but you can't un-soup it.\n\n**Brown your proteins and aromatics first.** This matters even more for plant-based cooking. Press and pan-fry tofu or tempeh before adding it to the slow cooker \u2014 it holds its shape and develops a much richer flavour. Same with onions and garlic: saut\u00e9 them in a little oil before they go in. Skipping this step is the most common reason slow cooker food tastes flat.\n\n**Timing for vegetables.** Hard vegetables (carrots, potatoes, beans) go in at the start. Softer ones (zucchini, spinach, tomatoes) go in for the last 30\u201360 minutes, otherwise they turn to mush.\n\n**For your cashew-based yogurt:** make sure your cashew base is fully cooled (room temperature) before adding the starter culture. If it's still warm, you'll kill the bacteria and get a thin, sour result instead of a proper set.\n\n**Beans and legumes:** if you're using dried beans in a slow cooker, pre-soak them overnight. They need a lot of liquid and a long cook, and adding them dry to other ingredients can make the whole pot under-seasoned as they absorb everything.\n\n**One specific recipe direction that fits what you're already planning:** a slow cooker black bean and sweet potato stew (you're already making tacos with those ingredients). Saut\u00e9 onions, garlic, and cumin in a pan, add sweet potatoes, canned black beans, a can of diced tomatoes, and just enough broth to barely cover. 6\u20137 hours on low. It's forgiving, scales well for your dinner parties, and the flavour deepens overnight if you make it ahead.\n\nWhat specifically has been going wrong \u2014 too much liquid, bland flavour, texture issues?", "autoeval_label": {"model": "openai/gpt-4o-2024-08-06", "label": true}}
